    "text": "Quadratic reciprocity makes \\(5\\) a square modulo \\(p\\); choosing the even representative \\(r\\) of the two roots and setting \\(n=r-1\\), \\(q=(r^2-5)/p\\), yields \\(n^2+2n-4=pq\\), with size and parity arguments giving \\(q\\le n-1\\) and \\(\\gcd(q,2(n-2))=1\\). A continuant identity then shows that the adjacent continuant is divisible by \\(q\\) but not by \\(p\\), so reduction cancels exactly the cofactor and leaves numerator \\(p\\).",
